AArch64 TicketLockAL3
(* Ticket lock (Promising-ARM PLDI'19 §7 "TL"), `ticketlock2.kl` with the
   ticket taken by LDADDAL (acquire-release) instead of LDADDA. Spin with
   LDAR on `owner` until it equals the ticket, critical section increments
   a counter, release with STLR of ticket+1 to `owner`. Three threads each
   take the lock once.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state. Expected: Always.
   Proved: `ticket_al_counter_envG` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/TicketAlPublic.lean)
   for all layouts and any number N of threads (N + 1 < 2^32), on the
   ticket environment with a release-kind ticket RMW `EnvGTDR` (the plan
   never releases at `next`; the dispenser hands each ticket's token out at
   the RMW; KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Write after load-acquire"). Whole image:
   concrete instance `ticket_al_counter_envG_concrete3` with `codeMatches`
   and `runnerMatches` in Promising/SLR/EnvG/ConcreteTicketAl.lean.
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t next`, `owner`, `counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner`, concrete
   `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_concrete3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64TicketRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64NoFaultDLocks.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64FaultFreeFixed.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `ticket_al_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean).
   Proved (TICKETAL): the promise-free fragment on a valid layout,
   `Live.TicketAl.ticket_al_live_pf [ValidLayout (layout tkWorkerAl)]`, concrete
   `ticket_al_live_pf_concrete`; with promises and semantic certification,
   `Live.TicketAl.ticket_al_live_sem` for every fuel, concrete
   `ticket_al_live_sem_concrete`; weak fairness alone is refuted,
   `ticketAlLiveWF_false`; the runner forms `ticket_al_live_{pf,sem}_runnerN`
   (Promising/LiveTicketAlThm.lean). `TicketAlLive fuel` for fuel >= 1 stays
   open, as for `ticketlock2.kl` (KNOWN_GAPS.md). *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t next=0; uint32_t owner=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=next; 0:X1=owner; 0:X2=counter;
1:X0=next; 1:X1=owner; 1:X2=counter;
2:X0=next; 2:X1=owner; 2:X2=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  MOV W6,#1
  LDADDAL W6,W3,[X0]
spin:
  LDAR W4,[X1]
  CMP W4,W3
  B.NE spin
  LDR W5,[X2]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X2]
  ADD W4,W3,#1
  STLR W4,[X1]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
